Allow the APIM Consumption tier: capacity must be 0, not 1.

WHY THIS EXISTS
  modules/apim/v3/apim.bicep hardcodes sku.capacity: 1. Every tier this lab
  was built for (Developer, Basic, Basicv2, Standard, Premium) accepts that.
  The Consumption tier does not: ARM rejects the deployment outright with

      MissingSkuTypeCapacity: For Consumption SKU Type capacity must be
      specified as 0.

  and there is no way around it from the outside - capacity is not a parameter
  of apim.bicep, and main.bicep only forwards apimSku. Note that
  `az deployment group validate` passes regardless; the failure only appears
  during a real deployment.

  We want Consumption because APIM is otherwise the dominant fixed cost of a
  demo environment that sits idle most of the time.

THIS IS A CUSTOMISATION, NOT A BUG REPORT
  Upstream never claimed to support Consumption in this lab, so there is
  nothing here for Microsoft to fix. That makes it different in kind from
  docs/05-upstream-issue-deployments-bicep.md, which documents a genuine
  upstream defect that IS reportable. Do not file this one.

  Keeping it as a patch rather than an edit in vendor/ is what preserves the
  property that vendor/ is upstream plus a known, reviewable delta.

APPLIED AUTOMATICALLY
  scripts/sync-vendor.ps1 applies every patch in this folder to the staged
  copy on each sync, before the build check, and fails the sync if one does
  not apply cleanly. Nothing needs to be re-applied by hand.

  If a future upstream revision touches this same line, the sync fails here.
  Re-cut the patch against the new file, or drop it if upstream has made
  capacity configurable on its own.

diff --git a/modules/apim/v3/apim.bicep b/modules/apim/v3/apim.bicep
index 394a497..e8ed272 100644
--- a/modules/apim/v3/apim.bicep
+++ b/modules/apim/v3/apim.bicep
@@ -83,7 +83,11 @@ resource apimService 'Microsoft.ApiManagement/service@2024-06-01-preview' = {
   location: location
   sku: {
     name: apimSku
-    capacity: 1
+    // LOCAL PATCH - not upstream. Applied by scripts/sync-vendor.ps1 from
+    // patches/apim-consumption-capacity.patch on every sync. The Consumption
+    // tier rejects any capacity other than 0 (MissingSkuTypeCapacity), and
+    // upstream hardcodes 1 because this lab never offered that tier.
+    capacity: apimSku == 'Consumption' ? 0 : 1
   }
   properties: {
     publisherEmail: publisherEmail
